# HOWTO: Set Up Windows VS Code with a Remote SSH Server

This guide walks through configuring **VS Code on Windows** to develop against a **remote Linux SSH server** using the Remote - SSH extension. It covers SSH login configuration, key-based authentication, the Remote - SSH extension, remote extension installation, and MCP (Model Context Protocol) server configuration.

---

## 1. Prerequisites

| Item | Where | Notes |
|------|-------|-------|
| VS Code | Windows 10/11 | Download from <https://code.visualstudio.com> |
| OpenSSH client | Windows | Usually pre-installed. Verify: `ssh -V` in PowerShell |
| Remote server access | — | Hostname/IP, username, and credentials (password or key) |
| Network reachability | — | VPN connected if the server is on a corporate network |

### Verify / install the Windows OpenSSH client

Open **PowerShell** and run:

```powershell
ssh -V
```

If it is missing, install it:

```powershell
# Run PowerShell as Administrator
Add-WindowsCapability -Online -Name OpenSSH.Client~~~~0.0.1.0
```

